<p><strong>Clinic appointment software for Nepal should schedule each practitioner and room together, keep a treatment course with the same practitioner, stop double-bookings, and record payments against each visit. It suits physiotherapy clinics, skin and aesthetic clinics and similar appointment-based practices.</strong></p>
<p>Clinics have a particular scheduling problem. A patient is rarely seen once. A physiotherapy course might be eight or ten visits over several weeks, ideally with the same therapist. A skin or aesthetic treatment might need a practitioner, a room and a device. If the diary does not know all of these, someone ends up rebooking by phone.</p>
<h2>What clinics need from appointment software</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Practitioner and room together.</strong> A slot is only free if both are free.</li>
<li><strong>Course continuity.</strong> Repeat visits should land with the same practitioner where possible. See <a href="/blog/physiotherapy-clinic-scheduling/">how physiotherapy clinics keep a course on schedule</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Online booking.</strong> Patients book outside opening hours, and reception stops being a phone line.</li>
<li><strong>Payment per visit.</strong> Cash, card and online recorded against the visit, with package balances where sessions are sold in bundles.</li>
<li><strong>Roles.</strong> Reception, practitioners and owners should see different things. See <a href="/features/role-based-access/">role-based access</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What it is not</h2>
<p>Scheduling software is not a medical records system. Zennly does not store clinical notes or diagnoses. It handles bookings, staff, payments and reporting, and you keep clinical records in whatever system your clinic already uses.</p>
<h2>Physiotherapy and beauty clinics are different</h2>
<p>A <a href="/solutions/physiotherapy/">physiotherapy clinic</a> cares most about courses and practitioner continuity. A <a href="/solutions/beauty-clinic/">beauty clinic</a> cares about practitioner and room availability, treatment packages and discount control. The same underlying tool can cover both if it books people, rooms and time together.</p>
<h2>Several branches</h2>
<p>Clinic groups in Kathmandu, Lalitpur and Pokhara can use one account for every branch and see one daily report. Practitioners who work across locations can be scheduled to transfer in advance. Read the <a href="/blog/manage-multiple-spa-salon-branches-nepal/">multi-branch checklist</a>.</p>

